  "contracts": [
    "Normal B1 profile places 26 jobs on TP0/1 and 13 on TP2–7; transfer this ownership to live ordinary DPs, zero gain on idle DPs. Keep every bank, output, dispatch fallback, lifetime and group. Six client cases in three service generations, no production frequency assumed.",
    "Slot host entries are pre-call observations on all 16 workers. Transfer this rank timing pattern relative to owning DP and number of graph waves to each stock run, with its own elapsed time. Sensitivities assume the specified net advance reaches each rank at graph entry. Unknown downstream per-rank tails may differ by the indicated spread and remain fixed within each counterfactual. Bounds may select different tails each wave. The full-transmission case bypasses the join. No post-TP and pre-TP credits are added.",
    "112 archived B4 rank windows bind each already-dual 24-row global / three-row local kernel to its exact launch API. The 13 subset is the global projection of the B4 trace, not a measurement of running a B1 caller. Grant both named device and node API times in series with zero replacement. Outer dispatch/guard time is separate. B4 whole-call median and its half are alternative sensitivity inputs.",
    "For graph-external lookup reuse, graph-internal raw-ID lookup and its SUM remain; eager prefill gets zero. Original embedding bank must have no independent reader on the chosen branch. Price the external local shard arithmetic, gather, mask and SUM as the change in latest group completion vs. latest entry minus local native task time. Use per-wave clock differences constrained by four observed TP8 collectives, retain all other device and scheduling work. All named local tasks fully exposed, unchanged other producers. An individual early consumer or a different schedule is outside this endpoint model.",
    "Per graph wave grant the largest eligible DP saving. Device plus CPU cases optimistically add the largest loop-local host cost to the device contribution even if they overlap. First-to-last launch span includes gaps. The next Fill/ZerosLike and the gap leading to it have no demonstrated removal from lookup reuse. Communication caller time outside those 14 launches is unpriced. Graph replay count and output wave cutoffs stay fixed.",
    "Ordinary duplicate lookup uses all three six-row external lookup groups on their own DP (two samples on DP0, one on DP1); cost transfers to the actual DP in each stock reference. Upper percentages are scenario results on those samples, not workload-wide bounds. Do not add these two candidates or credit changes in collective protocol, placement, inactive request branches or previous B4 service results."
  ],
